+# PG-BNN Physics-Guided Bayesian
 
-## Description
-Physics-Guided Bayesian Neural Network embedding thermodynamic/mechanical loss constraints with predictive uncertainty estimates.
+> **Category:** Physics-Informed & Explainable  
+> **Platform adapter:** `m18-pg-bnn`  
+> **Status:** integrated (BNN assembled from the repo's blocks)  
+> **Collection position:** model **16** of 25 (alphabetical)
 
-## Structure
+<!-- Generated from deployment/models.catalog.json - edit the catalog, not this file. -->
+
+A Bayesian neural network that predicts power under a P = tau * omega physics constraint and reports epistemic uncertainty by Monte Carlo sampling its own weights. It is the collection's answer to 'how much should we trust this model on conditions it has never seen'.
+
+## How this page fits the collection
+
+The WT-PM collection numbers its 25 repositories **alphabetically 01-25** - that is the number on this page - and gives each one a **task-based adapter id** (`m18-pg-bnn`) used by the platform registry, the `wt-pm` CLI and the fusion engine. Both are printed on every page so the ecosystem graph and the registry can be read against each other.
+
+- Repository: <https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-pg-bnn-wind-turbine>
+- Landing page: <https://rajaram-2005.github.io/wt-pm-pg-bnn-wind-turbine/>
+- Ecosystem graph: <https://rajaram-2005.github.io/wt-pm-lstm-scada-anomaly/ecosystem.html>
+- Platform architecture: <https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-lstm-scada-anomaly/blob/main/ARCHITECTURE.md>
+- Per-model table: <https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-lstm-scada-anomaly/blob/main/platform/docs/MODELS.md>
+
+## Model
+
+- `BayesianLinear / BNN blocks in model.py`
+- `Platform adapter assembles the full physics-guided model`
+
+| Block | Detail |
+|---|---|
+| Bayesian body | BayesianLinear layers sampling weights per forward pass - variational inference over parameters |
+| Physics constraint | Soft efficiency-adjusted mechanical-power penalty: P_electric ≈ 0.94 × τ × ω, with torque and power normalised in consistent kW units |
+| Readout | Monte-Carlo mean and epistemic weight spread; measured power, model residual and physics residual are returned as platform diagnostics |
+
+## Advanced concepts
+
+The ideas this model actually leans on - stated with their failure modes, not as marketing.
+
+### Epistemic versus aleatoric
+
+Monte-Carlo sampling over the variational weight posterior estimates an epistemic component; a fixed sample bank makes repeated requests comparable. It is not aleatoric sensor noise, and neither the spread nor the approximate mean ± 1.96σ band guarantees calibrated coverage.
+
+### Soft physics constraints
+
+The loss applies a soft penalty around P_electric ≈ 0.94 × τ × ω using consistent kW scaling. The measured-minus-physics residual is also exposed at inference, so an operator can compare the data fit with the mechanical cross-check without treating either as ground truth.
+
+### Physics and statistics disagree usefully
+
+The adapter reports predicted power, measured-minus-predicted error, efficiency-adjusted mechanical power and epistemic spread. Fusion uses m18 as an uncertainty-aware anomaly voter; its diagnostics are observations, not an oracle or a calibrated fault probability.
+
+## Platform contract
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Input (adapter view) | wind speed, ambient temperature, rotor speed, pitch, torque and measured power (the prediction target) |
+| Output (`WTDataSchema`) | WTDataSchema anomaly_score + uncertainty; /analyse physics.pg_bnn adds power prediction, MC spread and measured/model/physics residual diagnostics |
+| Record format | `wt-pm.platform.v1` |
+| Typical latency | 2500 ms |
+| Deployment targets | cloud |
+| Resource requirements | torch |
+| Fallback | none - this model is a leaf |
+| Subsystem focus | whole turbine |
+| Hermes tool | `anomaly (with confidence)` |
+
+Records follow the shared `WTDataSchema` (`wt-pm.platform.v1`): `timestamp`, `turbine_id` and `model_id` are required; every other field is optional, so a model fills in only what it honestly produces and the fusion layer can tell absence from a zero.
+
+## Platform layers
+
+| Layer | What this model does there |
+|---|---|
+| **Uncertainty** | Second of the two uncertainty emitters; enables inverse-variance weighting in the fusion engine |
+| **Physics** | Applies the efficiency-adjusted P=τω penalty during fitting and returns the measured-versus-physics residual under physics.pg_bnn |
+| **Hermes** | Hermes explain observations include the measured/predicted power, residuals and MC epistemic spread when m18 ran |
+| **RUL** | Physics-guided uncertainty propagates into m16's RUL posterior |
+
+Layers are described once, in the catalog, and referenced by every model that participates in them: fusion, calibrated uncertainty, drift and data trust, explainability, physics constraints, the safety gate, the evaluation protocol and the Hermes agent.
+
+## How it connects to the other 24
+
+**Receives from**
+
+- **07. Digital Twin Surrogate** (`m19-digital-twin`) - twin constraints for the PG-BNN
+
+**Feeds**
+
+- **15. Particle Filter RUL** (`m16-particle-filter-rul`) - physics-guided uncertainty into the RUL posterior
+- **24. XAI SHAP Interpretable** (`m21-xai-shap`) - explaining a physics-guided, uncertainty-carrying alert
+
+Related pages: [07 Digital Twin](https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-digital-twin-surrogate), [15 Particle Filter](https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-particle-filter-rul), [24 XAI SHAP](https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-xai-shap-interpretable)
+
