+<h1>PG-BNN Physics-Guided Bayesian</h1>
+<p class="lede">A Bayesian neural network that predicts power under a P = tau * omega physics constraint and reports epistemic uncertainty by Monte Carlo sampling its own weights. It is the collection's answer to 'how much should we trust this model on conditions it has never seen'.</p>
+<div class="cta">
+<a class="btn" href="https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-pg-bnn-wind-turbine">View on GitHub</a>
+<a class="btn ghost" href="https://rajaram-2005.github.io/wt-pm-lstm-scada-anomaly/ecosystem.html">25-model ecosystem graph</a>
+<a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-lstm-scada-anomaly/blob/main/ARCHITECTURE.md">Platform architecture</a>
+</div>
+</header>
+<p class="note">This page is generated from <code>deployment/models.catalog.json</code> in the reference repository, together with the other 24 model pages, so all 25 agree on numbering, contract and status.</p>
+<h2>Model</h2>
+<ul>
+<li><code>BayesianLinear / BNN blocks in model.py</code></li>
+<li><code>Platform adapter assembles the full physics-guided model</code></li>
+</ul>
+<table>
+<tr><th>Bayesian body</th><td>BayesianLinear layers sampling weights per forward pass - variational inference over parameters</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Physics constraint</th><td>Soft efficiency-adjusted mechanical-power penalty: P_electric ≈ 0.94 × τ × ω, with torque and power normalised in consistent kW units</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Readout</th><td>Monte-Carlo mean and epistemic weight spread; measured power, model residual and physics residual are returned as platform diagnostics</td></tr>
+</table>
+<h2>Advanced concepts</h2>
+<p class="note">The ideas this model actually leans on, each stated with its failure mode.</p>
+<div class="card">
+<h3>Epistemic versus aleatoric</h3>
+<p>Monte-Carlo sampling over the variational weight posterior estimates an epistemic component; a fixed sample bank makes repeated requests comparable. It is not aleatoric sensor noise, and neither the spread nor the approximate mean ± 1.96σ band guarantees calibrated coverage.</p>
+</div>
+<div class="card">
+<h3>Soft physics constraints</h3>
+<p>The loss applies a soft penalty around P_electric ≈ 0.94 × τ × ω using consistent kW scaling. The measured-minus-physics residual is also exposed at inference, so an operator can compare the data fit with the mechanical cross-check without treating either as ground truth.</p>
+</div>
+<div class="card">
+<h3>Physics and statistics disagree usefully</h3>
+<p>The adapter reports predicted power, measured-minus-predicted error, efficiency-adjusted mechanical power and epistemic spread. Fusion uses m18 as an uncertainty-aware anomaly voter; its diagnostics are observations, not an oracle or a calibrated fault probability.</p>
+</div>
+<h2>Platform contract</h2>
+<table>
+<tr><th>Input (adapter view)</th><td>wind speed, ambient temperature, rotor speed, pitch, torque and measured power (the prediction target)</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Output</th><td>WTDataSchema anomaly_score + uncertainty; /analyse physics.pg_bnn adds power prediction, MC spread and measured/model/physics residual diagnostics</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Record format</th><td><code>wt-pm.platform.v1</code></td></tr>
+<tr><th>Typical latency</th><td>2500 ms</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Deployment targets</th><td>cloud</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Requirements</th><td>torch</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Fallback</th><td>none - leaf model</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Subsystem focus</th><td>whole turbine</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Hermes tool</th><td><code>anomaly (with confidence)</code></td></tr>
+</table>
+<p class="note">Records follow the shared <code>WTDataSchema</code> (<code>wt-pm.platform.v1</code>). Only <code>timestamp</code>, <code>turbine_id</code> and <code>model_id</code> are required; absence is distinguishable from a zero.</p>
+<h2>Platform layers</h2>
+<table>
+<tr><th>Uncertainty</th><td>Second of the two uncertainty emitters; enables inverse-variance weighting in the fusion engine</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Physics</th><td>Applies the efficiency-adjusted P=τω penalty during fitting and returns the measured-versus-physics residual under physics.pg_bnn</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Hermes</th><td>Hermes explain observations include the measured/predicted power, residuals and MC epistemic spread when m18 ran</td></tr>
+<tr><th>RUL</th><td>Physics-guided uncertainty propagates into m16's RUL posterior</td></tr>
+</table>
+<h2>How it connects to the other 24</h2>
+<ul class="edges">
+<li><b>07. Digital Twin Surrogate</b> <span class="note">(m19-digital-twin)</span> &rarr; twin constraints for the PG-BNN</li>
+<li>&rarr; <b>15. Particle Filter RUL</b> <span class="note">(m16-particle-filter-rul)</span> - physics-guided uncertainty into the RUL posterior</li>
+<li>&rarr; <b>24. XAI SHAP Interpretable</b> <span class="note">(m21-xai-shap)</span> - explaining a physics-guided, uncertainty-carrying alert</li>
+</ul>
+<h2>Honest limits</h2><ul class="limits">
+<li>Variational approximation, not exact posterior inference</li>
+<li>Physics term is a soft penalty against the simulator's own physics</li>
+<li>MC epistemic spread and the approximate mean ± 1.96σ band are not calibrated coverage intervals</li>
+</ul>
+<p class="note">Fidelity: rung 1 of the fidelity ladder - simulator data, surrogate waveforms where stated, proxy RUL targets, simulator fault labels. Comparable within this collection, not field-validated turbine control.</p>
